      "hints": [
        "Introduce $u=3^x$ and clear the denominator in $(u+2)/(u-2)=8$.",
        "Solve the resulting linear equation for the positive value of $u$.",
        "Use $x=\\ln u/\\ln3$ and give the final result to exactly 3 decimal places."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Clear the denominator by multiplying both sides of $\\dfrac{3^x + 2}{3^x - 2} = 8$ by $(3^x - 2)$:\n$$3^x + 2 = 8(3^x - 2)$$",
        "Expand the right-hand side:\n$$3^x + 2 = 8(3^x) - 16$$",
        "Collect the terms involving $3^x$ on one side and constants on the other side:\n$$2 + 16 = 8(3^x) - 3^x$$\n$$18 = 7(3^x)$$",
        "Isolate $3^x$ by dividing by $7$:\n$$3^x = \\dfrac{18}{7}$$",
        "Take natural logarithms of both sides to solve for $x$:\n$$\\ln(3^x) = \\ln\\left(\\dfrac{18}{7}\\right)$$\n$$x\\ln 3 = \\ln 18 - \\ln 7$$",
        "Divide by $\\ln 3$:\n$$x = \\dfrac{\\ln 18 - \\ln 7}{\\ln 3} = \\dfrac{\\ln(18/7)}{\\ln 3}$$",
        "Evaluate numerically using logarithms:\n$$x \\approx \\dfrac{\\ln(2.571429)}{\\ln 3} \\approx \\dfrac{0.944462}{1.098612} \\approx 0.859687$$",
        "Round the answer to 3 decimal places:\n$$x = 0.860$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
